All four accepted findings are applied in the two in-box files; the deferred items (P3-4/5, P3-6, P3-7 remaining nits, P3-8) were not implemented, as instructed. Nothing staged, committed, merged, or pushed; no other file touched.

## Findings applied

| Finding | Change |
|---|---|
| **P2-1 (mid-frame retry)** | New test `a-half-read-frame-is-carried-across-a-retry`: half the worked example's datoms fill an open buffer → `drive` ends `:retry`/`:dao.stream/blocked` with the half-read frame asserted **inside the retry state** (dropping `:frame` now fails this) and zero writes; then the host appends the rest, seals, and `pump` re-steps to `:source-ended` with the destination holding exactly the full expected projection — the same graph, first half included. |
| **P2-2 (catch-all)** | New public `exception-diagnostic`: an ex-info with diagnostic data classifies `{:status :invalid-input, :diagnostic <ex-data>}`; anything else classifies `{:status :internal-error, :diagnostic {:rule :internal-error, :message (ex-message t)}}` — internal defects are no longer mislabeled input, and the status itself is `:internal-error`. The catch is now `#?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default)` — `Throwable` on the JVM per the `vm.cljc` precedent, so an `Error` is classified rather than escaping host-divergently. Docstring status list updated. Test `internal-defects-are-never-mislabeled-input` covers both branches with host-native plain throwables. |
| **P3-3 (alpha-equivalent adjacent graphs)** | The D4 adjacent-graphs fixture's second graph is now `(lam '[x] (lit 42))` — semantically different — plus an explicit `(not= projection-one projection-two)` assertion, so a bug replaying graph one's projection for graph two can no longer pass. |
| **P3-7 nit (docstring)** | `forward-step`'s docstring now states `:outcome` is carried **whenever** the last transport operation produced one, "including the blocked/full outcome a `:retry` hands back" — the false non-`:retry` restriction is gone. |

One fixture reality surfaced by the lanes: ClojureDart's `ex-message` on a plain `Exception` returns its `toString` (`"Exception: boom"`), so the internal-error test expects the host's own message per branch — the classification and status are identical on all hosts; only the message rendering is the host's, which is exactly what `:message (ex-message t)` prescribes.

